A f3-013 WRONG {'text': "To calculate how much energy a device uses in 4 minutes in **kilojoules (kJ)**, we need the **power rating** of the device (in watts or kilowatts) and the **time** (in seconds or minutes).\n\nHere's the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Energy (in joules)} = \\text{Power (in watts)} \\times \\text{Time (in seconds)}\n$$\n\nThen convert joules to **kilojoules** by dividing by 1000:\n\n$$\n\\text{Energy (in kJ)} = \\frac{\\text{Power (in watts)} \\times \\text{Time (in seconds)}}{1000}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Example:\nSuppose the device uses **500 watts** of power.\n\n- Time = 4 minutes = 4 × 60 = 240 seconds\n\n$$\n\\text{Energy} = \\frac{500 \\times 240}{1000} = \\frac{120,000}{1000} = 120 \\text{ kJ}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\nIf you provide the **power rating** (in watts) of the device, I can calculate the exact energy in **kilojoules** for 4 minutes. Otherwise, the general formula is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Energy (kJ)} = \\frac{\\text{Power (W)} \\times 240}{1000}\n$$\n\nLet me know the power, and I'll compute the exact value for you."}
