B f3-046 WRONG {'text': 'To find the **angular velocity** of a wheel in **rad/s**, we can use the following steps:\n\n---\n\n### **Given:**\n- **Diameter** of the wheel = 50 cm  \n- **Rotational speed (RPM)** = 600 revolutions per minute\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Convert RPM to revolutions per second (rev/s)**\n\n$$\n\\text{RPM} = 600 \\, \\text{rev/min}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{RPS} = \\frac{600}{60} = 10 \\, \\text{rev/s}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Convert revolutions per second to radians per second**\n\nSince 1 revolution = $2\\pi$ radians:\n\n$$\n\\omega = 10 \\, \\text{rev/s} \\times 2\\pi \\, \\text{rad/rev}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\omega = 20\\pi \\, \\text{rad/s}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: (Optional) Convert to numerical value (if needed)**\n\n$$\n\\omega \\approx 20 \\times 3.1416 \\approx 62.832 \\, \\text{rad/s}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{20\\pi \\, \\text{rad/s}} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\boxed{62.83 \\, \\text{rad/s}}\n$$'}
B f3-047 WRONG {'text': "To calculate the **centripetal acceleration** at the rim of an object (like a wheel, disk, or a rotating platform), you need to know:\n\n- The **radius** of the object (r), and  \n- The **angular velocity** (ω) or the **linear speed** (v) of the object at the rim.\n\nThe formula for **centripetal acceleration** is:\n\n$$\na_c = \\frac{v^2}{r} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a_c = \\omega^2 r\n$$\n\nWhere:\n- $ a_c $ is the centripetal acceleration in $ \\text{m/s}^2 $\n- $ v $ is the linear speed in $ \\text{m/s} $\n- $ r $ is the radius in meters\n- $ \\omega $ is the angular velocity in $ \\text{rad/s} $\n\n---\n\n### Example (if you provide values):\n\nSuppose:\n- Radius $ r = 0.5 \\, \\text{m} $\n- Angular velocity $ \\omega = 10 \\, \\text{rad/s} $\n\nThen:\n\n$$\na_c = \\omega^2 r = (10)^2 \\times 0.5 = 100 \\times 0.5 = 50 \\, \\text{m/s}^2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### If you can provide:\n- The **radius** and **angular speed** or **linear speed**, I can calculate the centripetal acceleration for you.\n\nLet me know the values, and I'll compute it for you!"}
