B f3-076 WRONG {'text': 'To find the **orbital speed** of a satellite orbiting Earth, we can use the formula for the orbital speed in a circular orbit:\n\n$$\nv = \\sqrt{\\frac{GM}{r}}\n$$\n\nWhere:\n\n- $ v $ is the orbital speed (in m/s),\n- $ GM $ is the standard gravitational parameter of Earth (given: $ 3.986 \\times 10^{14} \\, \\text{m}^3/\\text{s}^2 $),\n- $ r $ is the orbital radius (in meters).\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Convert radius to meters\nGiven:  \n$$\nr = 8000 \\, \\text{km} = 8,000,000 \\, \\text{m} = 8 \\times 10^6 \\, \\text{m}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Plug into the formula\n\n$$\nv = \\sqrt{\\frac{3.986 \\times 10^{14}}{8 \\times 10^6}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{3.986 \\times 10^{14}}{8 \\times 10^6}}\n$$\n\n$$\n= \\sqrt{4.9825 \\times 10^7} \\approx 7058.7 \\, \\text{m/s}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Convert to km/s\n\n$$\nv = \\frac{7058.7}{1000} = 7.0587 \\, \\text{km/s}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{7.06 \\, \\text{km/s}}\n$$\n\nThis is the **orbital speed** of a satellite orbiting Earth at a radius of 8000 km.'}
