B f3-081 WRONG {'text': 'To find the **wing loading**, which is defined as the **lift force per unit wing area**, we can use the **lift equation**:\n\n$$\nL = \\frac{1}{2} \\rho v^2 S C_L\n$$\n\nWhere:\n- $ L $ is the lift force (in Newtons),\n- $ \\rho $ is the air density (in kg/m³),\n- $ v $ is the velocity (in m/s),\n- $ S $ is the wing area (in m²),\n- $ C_L $ is the lift coefficient (dimensionless).\n\nWe are given:\n- $ \\text{Mass} = 5000 \\, \\text{kg} $\n- $ v = 80 \\, \\text{m/s} $\n- $ \\rho = 1.0 \\, \\text{kg/m}^3 $\n- $ C_L = 0.6 $\n- $ g = 9.81 \\, \\text{m/s}^2 $\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the lift force $ L $\n\nThe aircraft is flying **level**, so the lift force must equal the **weight** of the aircraft:\n\n$$\nL = \\text{Weight} = m \\cdot g = 5000 \\cdot 9.81 = 49050 \\, \\text{N}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the lift equation to find wing area $ S $\n\n$$\nL = \\frac{1}{2} \\rho v^2 S C_L\n$$\n\nSolve for $ S $:\n\n$$\nS = \\frac{2L}{\\rho v^2 C_L}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the known values:\n\n$$\nS = \\frac{2 \\cdot 49050}{1.0 \\cdot (80)^2 \\cdot 0.6}\n$$\n\n$$\nS = \\frac{98100}{1.0 \\cdot 6400 \\cdot 0.6} = \\frac{98100}{3840} \\approx 25.54 \\, \\text{m}^2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find the **wing loading**\n\nWing loading is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Wing Loading} = \\frac{L}{S} = \\frac{49050}{25.54} \\approx 1921 \\, \\text{N/m}^2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{1921 \\, \\text{N/m}^2}\n$$'}
