B f3-090 WRONG {'text': 'To find the **Mach number** for air, we use the formula:\n\n$$\nM = \\frac{v}{a}\n$$\n\nWhere:\n- $ M $ is the Mach number,\n- $ v $ is the flow velocity (in m/s),\n- $ a $ is the speed of sound in the fluid.\n\nThe speed of sound $ a $ in a gas is given by:\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{\\gamma R T}\n$$\n\nWhere:\n- $ \\gamma $ is the specific heat ratio (given as 1.4),\n- $ R $ is the specific gas constant (given as 287 J/(kg·K)),\n- $ T $ is the absolute temperature in Kelvin (given as 288 K).\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the speed of sound\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{1.4 \\times 287 \\times 288}\n$$\n\nFirst, compute the product inside the square root:\n\n$$\n1.4 \\times 287 = 401.8\n$$\n$$\n401.8 \\times 288 = 115,730.4\n$$\n\nNow take the square root:\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{115,730.4} \\approx 340.2 \\, \\text{m/s}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the Mach number\n\n$$\nM = \\frac{v}{a} = \\frac{150}{340.2} \\approx 0.441\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{M \\approx 0.44}\n$$\n\nSo, the Mach number for air at 288 K flowing at 150 m/s is approximately **0.44**.'}
